<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    Legion.Vehicles — the backend-agnostic Halcyon vehicle controller. SLICE 3 of the Jolt port.

    Ported BYTE-FOR-BYTE from Legion's donor tree; only THIS csproj is rewritten to RC conventions.
    The vehicle math is extracted VERBATIM from BulletSim's LegionVehicleDynamics.cs (itself the
    faithful Halcyon port), so BulletSim and Jolt share ONE source of truth for vehicle FEEL. The
    controller reads/writes physics ONLY through IVehicleBody — it links NEITHER OpenSim NOR any
    physics engine.

    Its only dependency is the OpenMetaverse math types (Vector3/Quaternion/Utils). The RC provides
    those GLOBALLY via Directory.Build.props (vendored OpenMetaverse.Types); Legion referenced the
    same library under its old name "OpenMetaverseTypes", so that HintPath simply drops away here.

    DEPENDENCY GRAPH (no cycle): the LegionJolt MODULE consumes BOTH Legion.Vehicles and Legion.Physics;
    Vehicles and Physics are INDEPENDENT siblings (Vehicles does NOT reference Physics; Physics does NOT
    reference Vehicles). Slice 4's JoltVehicleBody (in the module) implements IVehicleBody to bridge the
    controller onto the backend.

    ImplicitUsings disabled to match the donor (files carry explicit usings).
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <AssemblyName>Legion.Vehicles</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Legion.Vehicles</RootNamespace>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Deterministic>true</Deterministic>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>false</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
